WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:13.260
Today we are going to give a really hard time&nbsp;
to a robot. Look at this, and this. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:19.740
Google’s robots are getting smarter and smarter&nbsp;
every year, for instance, we talked about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:26.760
robot assistant where we can say “please help&nbsp;
me, I have spilled the coke”, and then…it creates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:34.980
a cunning plan! It tries to throw out the coke&nbsp;
can, well, almost. Then, it brings us a sponge.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.800
And, if we’ve been reading research papers all&nbsp;
day and we feel a little tired, if we tell it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.680
it can bring us a water bottle, hand it&nbsp;
to us, and can even bring us an apple.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.940
A different robot of theirs&nbsp;
has learned to drive itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:00.840
also understands English, and can thus,&nbsp;
take instructions from us and find its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.060
way around. And these instructions&nbsp;
can be really nasty, like this one.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:11.400
However, there is one thing that&nbsp;
neither of these previous robots can do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.300
but this new one can. Let’s see what it is.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.380
Let’s ask for a soda again, and once&nbsp;
again, it comes up with a cunning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:28.740
plan. Go to the coke can, pick it up, and&nbsp;
haha! Checkmate, little robot! Now what?&nbsp;

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:35.520
Now comes the coolest part! It realizes that&nbsp;
it has failed, and now, change of plans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:43.351
it says the following: there is no coke, but&nbsp;
there is an orange soda. Is that okay with us?

00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:49.620
So, are we going to be kind? No-no, we are&nbsp;
going to be a little picky here and say no and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:56.280
ask for a lime soda instead! The robot probably&nbsp;
thinks, oh goodness, a change of plans again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:03.300
let’s look for that lime soda. And it is, of&nbsp;
course, really far away to give it a hard time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:11.400
so let’s see what it does…wow, look at that!&nbsp;
It found it in the other end of the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:17.820
recognized that this is indeed the&nbsp;
soda, picks it up, and we are done!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:24.900
So cool! The amenities at the Google&nbsp;
headquarters are truly next level. I love it.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:32.460
This was super fun, so you know what? Let’s try&nbsp;
another task. Let’s ask it to put the coke can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:40.560
into the top drawer. Will it succeed? Well,&nbsp;
look at that! The human operator cannot wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:48.300
to mess with this little robot, and aha!&nbsp;
Sure enough, that drawer is not opening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:55.740
So, is this a problem? Well, first, the robot&nbsp;
recognized that this was not successful, but now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:02.940
the environment has changed, the pesky human&nbsp;
is gone, so, it tries again. And this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:08.760
the drawer opens, in goes the coke can,&nbsp;
it holds the drawer with both fingers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:16.380
and now I just need a gentle&nbsp;
little push, and, bravo! Good job!

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:20.340
So we tried to confuse this robot&nbsp;
by messing up the environment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:27.420
and it did really well, but now, get this,&nbsp;
what if we mess with its brain instead?&nbsp;

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:35.520
How? Well, check this out. Let’s ask it to throw&nbsp;
away the snack on the counter, it asks which one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:42.600
and to which our answer is of course, not the&nbsp;
apple, no-no. Let’s mess with it a little more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:51.120
Our answer is that we changed our mind, so please&nbsp;
throw away something on the table instead. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:57.360
now as it approaches the table, let’s try to&nbsp;
mess with it again, you know what? Nevermind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:03.120
just finish the previous task instead.&nbsp;
And it finally goes there and grabs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:09.180
the apple. We tried really hard, but we&nbsp;
could not mess with this guy. So cool!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:16.740
So, a new robot that understands English, can&nbsp;
move around, make a plan, and most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:25.200
it a can come up with a plan B when plan A&nbsp;
fails. Wow. A little personal assistant. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.420
pace of progress in AI research is nothing&nbsp;
short of amazing. What a time to be alive!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:35.160
So, what would you use this for?&nbsp;
Let me know in the comments below!

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.560
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

